<!--
  RUT_ScarlandsItems.xml                 UtinniPatches - COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1

  RUT_GlowerCrust — the harvested product of RUT_Glower
  (RUT_ScarlandsFlora.xml). ParentName="ResourceBase" (same parent Steel/
  RUT_FungalSoil use — a plain tradeable raw resource, alwaysHaulable/
  Sellable by inheritance). Carries BOTH uses the sheet's §4 text names
  ("harvestable as radiogenic fuel and pigment") in one item rather than
  two, the same "one commission, one property, not four bespoke items"
  discipline the poison_forest wave's toxic-meat pass used — there is no
  separate fuel-vs-pigment mechanic named anywhere yet to justify splitting
  it, and splitting speculatively would be inventing scope this pass does
  not own.

  Real radiological handling (dose exposure on harvest/handling, the
  "glower-fuel harvest" gameplay loop the roster's own mechanic_load names)
  is deferred to SCARLANDS_MECHANICS_2 — this item lands as a plain sellable
  raw resource now, same "def first, mechanic follows" precedent.

  Art: no existing render found (checked infrastructure/artpipe/
  {done,pending,registry.jsonl} for "glower" — clean). One job filed this
  pass, rutglowercrust_v1 (infrastructure/artpipe/pending/
  rutglowercrust_v1.json).
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RUT_GlowerCrust</defName>
    <label>glower crust</label>
    <description>A scraped-up chunk of black radiotrophic varnish, still faintly warm. Burned, it makes a crude, hot fuel; reduced to ash, it makes a pigment nothing else on the planet can match — deep, matte black that doesn't fade. Handling too much of it too long is its own kind of story.</description>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <graphicData>
      <!-- Job rutglowercrust_v1, filed this pass. Pending until the daemon lands it. -->
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RUT_GlowerCrust</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <stackLimit>50</stackLimit>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>4.5</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.6</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.5</Flammability>
      <Beauty>-1</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <alwaysHaulable>true</alwaysHaulable>
    <resourceReadoutPriority>Middle</resourceReadoutPriority>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
